## Project Organization Pattern (Full Pipeline — for model development / multi-cohort studies)

Use this pattern when the project involves: training + validation cohorts, multiple derived scores/clocks, model serialization, or ≥7 pipeline steps. Reference implementation: a biological-age model project.

### Script Naming Convention

```
00_setup.R               # Shared utilities, paths, packages (sourced by all)
01_data_import.R         # Download/parse raw data → data/raw/
02_clean.R               # Merge, recode, filter → data/processed/*_clean_*.rds
03–04_*.R                # Compute derived scores (e.g., PhenoAge, AnthropoAge)
05_model_train.R         # Train model on training cohort → *_model_*.rds
06_model_validate.R      # Apply model to validation cohort → *_final_*.rds
07_main_analysis.R       # Primary analysis (Cox, classification, etc.)
08_tables_figures.R      # Publication tables & figures
09_sensitivity.R         # Sensitivity, subgroup, additional analyses
run_all.R                # Master pipeline runner
```

### Rules

- Every script starts with `source("R/00_setup.R")`
- Scripts communicate **only** via date-stamped `.rds` files in `data/processed/`
- `latest_file(dir, pattern)` auto-selects newest matching file — no hardcoded dates
- Master runner (`run_all.R`) calls each script via `source()` wrapped in `tryCatch()`
- Suffixed numbers for sub-steps: `05_2_sensitivity.R`

### 00_setup.R Template

```r
proj_dir    <- detect_proj_dir()
data_dir    <- file.path(proj_dir, "data")
raw_dir     <- file.path(data_dir, "raw")
proc_dir    <- file.path(data_dir, "processed")
output_dir  <- file.path(proj_dir, "output")
tables_dir  <- file.path(output_dir, "tables")
pub_dir     <- file.path(output_dir, "tables", "publication")
figures_dir <- file.path(output_dir, "figures")

stamp <- format(Sys.Date(), "%y%m%d")

excel_name  <- function(file) paste0(file, "_", stamp, ".xlsx")
rds_name    <- function(file) paste0(file, "_", stamp, ".rds")
latest_file <- function(dir, pattern) {
  files <- list.files(dir, pattern = pattern, full.names = TRUE)
  if (length(files) == 0) stop("No files matching '", pattern, "' in ", dir)
  files[which.max(file.mtime(files))]
}

## ---- intermediate I/O: single source of truth (proc_dir), drift-proof ----
## Scripts NEVER write .RData/.rds intermediates to output_dir. Use these helpers so the
## directory cannot drift. envir = parent.frame() preserves save()/load() named-object semantics
## (objects resolved in / loaded into the CALLING script's environment — pass named vars, e.g.
## save_step(df03, name = "df_step03"); a bare expression like save_step(data.frame(...)) fails,
## which is R's save() limitation, not the helper).
step_path <- function(name) file.path(proc_dir, paste0(name, "_", stamp, ".RData"))
save_step <- function(..., name) {
  f <- step_path(name); save(..., file = f, envir = parent.frame())
  message("Saved: ", f); invisible(f)
}
load_step <- function(pattern) {
  f <- latest_file(proc_dir, pattern); load(f, envir = parent.frame())
  message("Loaded: ", basename(f)); invisible(f)
}
## guard: intermediates must not leak into output/ (output/ = tables + figures only)
.stray <- list.files(output_dir, pattern = "^df_step.*\\.RData$|_(clean|score|model|final)_.*\\.rds$")
if (length(.stray)) warning("intermediate files found in output/ (belong in data/processed/): ",
                            paste(.stray, collapse = ", "))
```

**Directory contract (NON-NEGOTIABLE):** `data/processed/` = intermediates (date-stamped `.RData`/`.rds`),
`output/` = **코드가 다시 만들어내는 것**(표·그림), `logs/` = run logs.
저작물(원고·발표덱·포스터·투고 패키지)은 `output/` 밑에 **두지 않는다** — 아래 「저작물 폴더」 절.
Never write intermediates or logs into `output/`. Define `proc_dir` in setup and route all
intermediate I/O through `save_step()`/`load_step()` so a script cannot silently write to the wrong
place; the guard above flags leaks on every source. (2026-07-12, one project: `proc_dir` was defined
but unused — 27 sites wrote/read `df_step*.RData` in `output/` — fixed by routing through helpers.)

**Build-script portability:** Python build scripts (research brief / manuscript totale / PPT) compute
`ROOT` from their own location — `ROOT = str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[N])` (N = depth below
root) — and NEVER hardcode an absolute machine path. This keeps them runnable on any machine and
from any cwd. Verify by rebuilding after the change.

### Directory Structure

```
project_root/
├── R/
│   ├── 00_setup.R
│   ├── 01–09_*.R
│   └── run_all.R
├── data/
│   ├── raw/                   # Downloaded source data (cached)
│   └── processed/             # Date-stamped intermediate RDS
│       ├── *_clean_YYMMDD.rds
│       ├── *_model_YYMMDD.rds
│       └── *_final_YYMMDD.rds
├── output/                    # 지워도 되는 것 — run_all.R 이 되살린다
│   ├── tables/
│   │   └── publication/       # Manuscript-ready tables (.xlsx)
│   └── figures/               # Publication plots (.png, 300 dpi)
└── manuscript/                # 저작물. presentation/ poster/ submission/ 도 최상위
```

### Data Flow

```
01 → raw/*.rds
02 → processed/*_clean_*.rds
03–04 → processed/*_score_*.rds (cumulative columns)
05 → processed/*_model_*.rds (trained model as named list)
06 → processed/*_final_*.rds (all scores + classifications)
07 → output/tables/*.xlsx
08 → output/tables/publication/*.xlsx + output/figures/fig*.png
09 → output/tables/publication/tableS*.xlsx + output/figures/figS*.png
```

### Model Object Convention

Store trained models as a named list in a single `.rds`:
```r
model <- list(
  fit_M = model_object, fit_F = model_object,  # sex-stratified fits
  selected_vars = character_vector,
  formula = formula_object,
  inv_params_M = list(s, b0, b1),              # inversion parameters
  var_map = data.frame(...)                     # variable mapping
)
saveRDS(model, file.path(proc_dir, rds_name("model")))
```

### Publication Output Naming

- Main: `main_table1_*`, `fig1_*`, `fig2_*`
- Supplementary: `tableS1_*`, `figS1_*`
- All date-stamped

