## Publication Table Pattern

When building regression/summary tables for manuscripts, use the `header_row` + `build_row` pattern:

```
Variable                    Crude              Model 1 (adjusted)
Active use
  No                        1.00 (ref)         1.00 (ref)
  Yes                       1.xx (x.xx-x.xx)*  1.xx (x.xx-x.xx)*
```

**Helper functions:**
```r
header_row <- function(label, col_names = c("Variable", "Crude", "Model 1 (adjusted)")) {
  out <- as.data.frame(matrix("", nrow = 1, ncol = length(col_names)))
  names(out) <- col_names
  out[[1L]] <- label
  out
}

build_row <- function(label, crude_str, adj_str) {
  data.frame(
    Variable = label,
    Crude = crude_str,
    `Model 1 (adjusted)` = adj_str,
    stringsAsFactors = FALSE, check.names = FALSE
  )
}

# Assemble:
table_formatted <- do.call(rbind, list(
  header_row("Active use"),
  build_row("  No",  crude_no,  adj_no),
  build_row("  Yes", crude_yes, adj_yes)
))
```

**RData standalone fallback:** when a table script may be run from a saved `.RData` without the full pipeline, add fallbacks for objects only defined upstream:
```r
if (!exists("Zvar")) {
  Zvar <- c("sex", "age", "edu", ...)  # project-specific default
}
```

